  "answer_core": "I wouldn’t commit to 15% equity, a CTO title, and a board seat this Friday. Those are long‑term governance and ownership moves that only make sense once you know whether the partnership actually strengthens the company or concentrates risk around Marcus.\n\nFriday should be a direct, structured conversation about a staged path. Make clear that there is a real route to major upside for him, but it has to be tied to demonstrated impact. Set a short, defined window to test whether he delivers the core platform work, whether that work proves revenue‑relevant, whether team continuity improves rather than depends more on him, whether knowledge transfer happens, and whether his behavior fits the governance standards you need. Be explicit about what proving those things would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both a premature, irreversible commitment and the ambiguity of a vague “later” that could push him away. You give him a credible path forward, but one anchored in evidence and company health.",
